    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Question\n\nIs there a way to write a function or user command that enters a submode? \r\n\r\nI added to my config a submode for moving between git hunks and staging them. I'm trying to add a way to open nvim already in this submode, for smoother work with lazygit.\r\n\r\nI've tried using nvim_input to input submode's prefix, or to read first keypress and input prefix..keypress, but this doesn't trigger mini.clue so it doesn't leave me in submode",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.clue</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a way to write a function or user command that enters a submode?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I added to my config a submode for moving between git hunks and staging them. I'm trying to add a way to open nvim already in this submode, for smoother work with lazygit.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've tried using nvim_input to input submode's prefix, or to read first keypress and input prefix..keypress, but this doesn't trigger mini.clue so it doesn't leave me in submode</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.clue\nQuestion\nIs there a way to write a function or user command that enters a submode?\nI added to my config a submode for moving between git hunks and staging them. I'm trying to add a way to open nvim already in this submode, for smoother work with lazygit.\nI've tried using nvim_input to input submode's prefix, or to read first keypress and input prefix..keypress, but this doesn't trigger mini.clue so it doesn't leave me in submode",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
