    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-02-11T10:20:19Z",
    "comment_count": 2,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I've tried using nvim_input to input submode's prefix, or to read first keypress and input prefix..keypress, but this doesn't trigger mini.clue so it doesn't leave me in submode\r\n\r\nUsing `vim.api.nvim_input` works for me. For example, with the [`submode_resize` enabled](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c3e3cc925217b59f1b39264c6981eb1692a86466/doc/mini-clue.txt#L436-L456) interactively executing `:lua vim.api.nvim_input('<C-w>>')` increases width once and starts the submode.\r\n\r\nWhat 'mini.clue' setup do you have and what `nvim_input` input have you tried?\r\n\r\n> I'm trying to add a way to open nvim already in this submode, for smoother work with lazygit.\r\n\r\nThis may be another source of issues. For example, make sure that 'mini.clue' is not lazy loaded (i.e. is set up before `nvim_input()` call).",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've tried using nvim_input to input submode's prefix, or to read first keypress and input prefix..keypress, but this doesn't trigger mini.clue so it doesn't leave me in submode</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Using <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.api.nvim_input</code> works for me. For example, with the <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c3e3cc925217b59f1b39264c6981eb1692a86466/doc/mini-clue.txt#L436-L456\"><code class=\"notranslate\">submode_resize</code> enabled</a> interactively executing <code class=\"notranslate\">:lua vim.api.nvim_input('&lt;C-w&gt;&gt;')</code> increases width once and starts the submode.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What 'mini.clue' setup do you have and what <code class=\"notranslate\">nvim_input</code> input have you tried?</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm trying to add a way to open nvim already in this submode, for smoother work with lazygit.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This may be another source of issues. For example, make sure that 'mini.clue' is not lazy loaded (i.e. is set up before <code class=\"notranslate\">nvim_input()</code> call).</p>",
            "bodyText": "I've tried using nvim_input to input submode's prefix, or to read first keypress and input prefix..keypress, but this doesn't trigger mini.clue so it doesn't leave me in submode\n\nUsing vim.api.nvim_input works for me. For example, with the submode_resize enabled interactively executing :lua vim.api.nvim_input('<C-w>>') increases width once and starts the submode.\nWhat 'mini.clue' setup do you have and what nvim_input input have you tried?\n\nI'm trying to add a way to open nvim already in this submode, for smoother work with lazygit.\n\nThis may be another source of issues. For example, make sure that 'mini.clue' is not lazy loaded (i.e. is set up before nvim_input() call).",
