        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25957685?v=4",
                "login": "aShabat",
                "resourcePath": "/aShabat",
                "url": "https://github.com/aShabat"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Sorry for bothering again, but there is one thing I don't understand.\r\nI made this example script\r\n```\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', ' nn', 'j')\r\nrequire('mini.clue').setup{\r\n    triggers = {\r\n        {mode = 'n', keys = ' n'},\r\n    },\r\n    clues = {\r\n        {mode = 'n', keys = ' nn', postkeys = ' n'},\r\n    },\r\n}\r\n```\r\nAfter this, if I run `vim.api.nvim_input' n'` it does wait for next input and works like a submode. But if I run `vim.api.nvim_input' nn'` it moves down once, but doesn't stay in submode.\r\n\r\nAs you said, submode_resize works as expected, but for some reason submodes that I create myself don't.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Sorry for bothering again, but there is one thing I don't understand.<br>\nI made this example script</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.keymap.set('n', ' nn', 'j')\nrequire('mini.clue').setup{\n    triggers = {\n        {mode = 'n', keys = ' n'},\n    },\n    clues = {\n        {mode = 'n', keys = ' nn', postkeys = ' n'},\n    },\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">vim.keymap.set('n', ' nn', 'j')\nrequire('mini.clue').setup{\n    triggers = {\n        {mode = 'n', keys = ' n'},\n    },\n    clues = {\n        {mode = 'n', keys = ' nn', postkeys = ' n'},\n    },\n}\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">After this, if I run <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.api.nvim_input' n'</code> it does wait for next input and works like a submode. But if I run <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.api.nvim_input' nn'</code> it moves down once, but doesn't stay in submode.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As you said, submode_resize works as expected, but for some reason submodes that I create myself don't.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Sorry for bothering again, but there is one thing I don't understand.\nI made this example script\nvim.keymap.set('n', ' nn', 'j')\nrequire('mini.clue').setup{\n    triggers = {\n        {mode = 'n', keys = ' n'},\n    },\n    clues = {\n        {mode = 'n', keys = ' nn', postkeys = ' n'},\n    },\n}\n\nAfter this, if I run vim.api.nvim_input' n' it does wait for next input and works like a submode. But if I run vim.api.nvim_input' nn' it moves down once, but doesn't stay in submode.\nAs you said, submode_resize works as expected, but for some reason submodes that I create myself don't.",
